cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VYRA or its results in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "VYRA: Testing Yielding Resistance in Hybrid Post-Quantum Constructions by Failure Injection"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Carrington"
    family-names: "Junior"
    affiliation: "Market Standard, LLC"
  - given-names: "Trey"
    family-names: "Huffine"
    affiliation: "Market Standard, LLC"
repository-code: "https://github.com/marketstandard/VYRA"
url: "https://github.com/marketstandard/VYRA"
abstract: >-
  VYRA is a research-stage hybrid post-quantum cryptography library in Rust
  (ML-KEM with HQC, ML-DSA with Ed25519 or SLH-DSA) together with a
  failure-injection experiment that deliberately breaks one component and
  attacks the combined scheme. It is a research prototype and is not for
  protecting real data.
keywords:
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - hybrid KEM
  - composite signatures
  - KEM combiner
  - failure injection
  - ML-KEM
  - HQC
  - ML-DSA
  - SLH-DSA
  - Rust
license: "MIT OR Apache-2.0"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-19"
